// Title: Harvesting Of Wifi Credentials Via Netsh.EXE
// Sigma ID: 42b1a5b8-353f-4f10-b256-39de4467faff
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades), oscd.community
// Date: 2020-04-20 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: discovery, credential-access, T1040
// Description: Detect the harvesting of wifi credentials using netsh.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.malwarebytes.com/threat-analysis/2020/04/new-agenttesla-variant-steals-wifi-credentials/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_netsh_wifi_credential_harvesting.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\netsh.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "netsh.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "wlan" and ProcessCommandLine contains " s" and ProcessCommandLine contains " p" and ProcessCommandLine contains " k" and ProcessCommandLine contains "=clear")
